<%# console.privacy-policy-guide — privacy-policy-guide.php, modernized. h1 LITERAL. -%>
<% @page_title = "Privacy Policy Guide" %>
<h1 class="wp-heading-inline">Privacy Policy Guide</h1>
<hr class="wp-header-end">

<p>The Privacy Policy Guide helps you write a privacy policy for your site. Set the page that holds
your policy under <%= link_to "Settings › Privacy", "/console/settings/privacy" %>, then edit that
page to describe what data your site collects and how it is used.</p>

<h2>Suggested sections</h2>
<ul>
  <li>What personal data this site collects and why (comments, contact forms, analytics).</li>
  <li>How long the site retains data, and who it is shared with.</li>
  <li>The rights a visitor has over their data, and how to exercise them
      (see <%= link_to "Export Personal Data", "/console/tools/export-personal-data" %> and
      <%= link_to "Erase Personal Data", "/console/tools/erase-personal-data" %>).</li>
</ul>
<p class="description">This guidance is the rebuild&#8217;s own (DEV-009). WordPress&#8217;s project-authored
suggested-text was not migrated.</p>
